# Implementation Plan: Proximity Auto-Hitting, Progressive Speed Ramp & Full-Stack Leaderboard

This plan outlines the architecture and changes required to transform the hitting mechanics of the Ganesha Volleyball Game to be strictly proximity-based (eliminating manual spacebar hitting), add smooth progressive speed acceleration to the Modak ball, expand the landing zone reticle, and deliver a lightweight full-stack player authentication and leaderboard system.

All existing court dimensions, Modak geometries, and Mushak procedural models will remain strictly intact.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Key Gameplay & Architecture Confirmations**:
> 1. **Auto-Hit Mechanics**: The hit impulse automatically triggers the instant the Player Mushak steps into the expanded landing reticle / collision zone while the Modak is at hit altitude. No manual spacebar press will be needed during rallies.
> 2. **Serving Phase**: Serving can be initiated either by pressing `Space`, walking into the serve zone, or clicking a convenient "SERVE" UI button, ensuring zero frustration while keeping rally hits strictly automatic.
> 3. **Backend Stack**: We will implement an Express.js backend in `server/` leveraging Node 24's native SQLite engine (`node:sqlite`) with persistent file storage and zero external C++ compiler dependencies. We will configure Vite's dev server proxy so all `/api/*` routes route seamlessly to the backend.

