## Proposed Changes

### 1. Physics & Gameplay Loop (Auto-Hitting & Speed Ramping)

#### [MODIFY] [constants.js](file:///c:/Users/Saksham/OneDrive/Desktop/ganesha-vollyball-game/src/game/constants.js)
- Expand `RETICLE_TRIGGER_RADIUS` from `2.25` to `3.85` (~1.7x expansion).
- Expand `HIT_RADIUS` from `1.9` to `3.2` (~1.7x expansion).
- Define speed ramp constants:
  - `INITIAL_SPEED_MULTIPLIER = 0.65`
  - `MAX_SPEED_MULTIPLIER = 1.50`
  - `SPEED_RAMP_PER_HIT = 0.04` (+4% speed per volley hit)
  - `SPEED_RAMP_PER_5S = 0.03` (+3% speed every 5 seconds of active rally)

#### [MODIFY] [GameController.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Saksham/OneDrive/Desktop/ganesha-vollyball-game/src/components/GameController.jsx)
- **Proximity-Based Auto-Hitting**:
  - Replace manual spacebar hit trigger with an automatic trigger: when Player Mushak enters the expanded reticle zone (`distToReticle <= RETICLE_TRIGGER_RADIUS` or `distToBall <= HIT_RADIUS`) and the ball is within playable altitude and heading to player side.
  - Apply instant smooth leap impulse (`playerVelYRef.current = 4.2`) and fire hit shockwave effect.
  - Dynamically calculate shot power and target based on player's position, movement direction (A/D lateral bias), and distance to reticle center.
  - Implement a 0.35s hit cooldown / lastHitter guard to prevent accidental multi-frame double hits.
- **Progressive Ball Speed Ramping**:
  - Maintain `speedMultiplier` state (starting at `0.65`).
  - Scale ball physics time-step by `speedMultiplier` (`ballDelta = delta * speedMultiplier`).
  - Increment `speedMultiplier` by `+0.04` on every hit (player and opponent) and `+0.03` every 5 seconds of active play, capped at `1.50`.
  - Reset `speedMultiplier` back to `0.65` upon ball grounding, point scored, or match restart.
  - Propagate speed multiplier and hit count to HUD for live speed display.

#### [MODIFY] [LandingReticle.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Saksham/OneDrive/Desktop/ganesha-vollyball-game/src/components/LandingReticle.jsx)
- Substantially expand the visual footprint of the reticle to match the new 1.7x trigger zone:
  - Expand outer ring radius from `0.52` to `0.85`.
  - Expand trigger aura radius from `0.92` to `1.55`.
  - Enhance visual feedback (smooth pulsing glow when the player enters the zone).

